# Sample Vite scan file for Heavy-Rental/heavy-rental-react-web-portal
# Copy to the React repo root as `.env.production` (or `docs/samples/.env.production`).
#
# This is NOT the Vite mode file used for GHCR. Release Packaging:
#   1. Seeds/scans this file (fails on sk_, lab hosts, REST/Haystack URLs).
#   2. Runs `npx tsc -b` then `npx vite build --mode api`.
# `--mode api` loads `.env.api` (and `.env`), not `.env.production`.
# Process env then empties VITE_API_TARGET / VITE_* backends so the SPA
# uses same-origin `/api`. CD mounts that path → SM REST_BASE_URL.
#
# Optional Stripe pk_ is baked from Environment academy
# VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY (Packaging `environment: academy`), not from
# this file. A pk_ here is allowed; sk_ / whsec_ fail the scan.
#
# Do NOT:
#   - COPY this file into the nginx image (Release generates try_files only)
#   - Put REST_BASE_URL, Haystack hosts, RDS, JWT, AWS keys, or Stripe sk_
#   - Set VITE_API_TARGET / VITE_REST_* / VITE_HAYSTACK_* to a hostname
#     (empty or a same-origin path like /api is OK)
#   - Expect GitHub VITE_* (other than academy pk_ at Packaging) to change
#     the running SPA. CD overlay of pk_ writes guest .env only; the browser
#     still uses the key baked at Release.
#
# Ownership (ADR 0008):
#   Infra sync-secrets → heavy-rental/portal → guest .env (REST_BASE_URL, pk_)
#   Portal Environment academy / AWS_ACTUAL → CD overlay of pk_ onto guest .env
#   This file → Release scan input only

# Empty backends: SPA uses same-origin /api (CD mounts REST_BASE_URL).
VITE_API_URL=
VITE_REST_URL=
VITE_REST_BASE_URL=
VITE_HAYSTACK_URL=
VITE_HAYSTACK_BASE_URL=
